  "articleBody": "Home additions are exciting, but they can definitely test your patience with their timelines. If your project seems to be dragging, it’s often due to a few common factors. First, underestimating the schedule is a big one; additions typically take much longer than simple interior refreshes, with kitchen additions sometimes stretching to 12-16 weeks and major whole-house remodels with additions taking 6-10 months. Second, poor coordination among different trades can cause significant delays, as one step often depends on another. Finally, structural surprises or unexpected material shortages can push deadlines back, so always allow extra time for potential delays. That’s where a professional like HH Remodeling LLC really shines. With their expertise in managing complex trade sequencing and permit handling, they can help you navigate these challenges. Clear communication and experienced project management are vital to keeping your addition project moving forward and avoiding unnecessary frustration.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}